433 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 241 0 R
/E (The AutoML paradigm began with early work on combined algorithm selection and hyperparameter optimization \(CASH\). Thornton et al. \(2013\) introduced Auto- WEKA, the first system to frame AutoML as a structured CASH problem solvable by Bayesian optimization. Feurer et al. \(2015\) extended this with Auto-sklearn, incorporating meta-learning and ensemble construction on top of scikit-learn pipelines. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
434 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 241 0 R
/E (Google's AutoML systems brought the concept to commercial scale, optimizing neural architecture search \(NAS\) for image classification. H2O AutoML \(LeDell & Poirier, 2020\) provided accessible tree-based ensemble automation. TPOT \(Olson et al., 2016\) introduced genetic programming for pipeline optimization. Despite their achievements, most of these systems still rely on simple train-test splits or single-level cross-validation, leaving them vulnerable to optimistic bias. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
