581 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 251 0 R
/E (The most pervasive source of inflated AutoML performance is the misuse of the validation set. Consider the following common workflow: split data 80/20, train 100 model configurations on the 80% split, evaluate all on the 20% validation split, select the best. The reported validation score is biased because the selection process used the validation set as a selection criterion. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
582 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 251 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
583 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 251 0 R
/E (A secondary source of leakage is preprocessing leakage: fitting a StandardScaler, SimpleImputer, or SelectKBest on the full dataset \(including validation fold\) before cross-validation allows test statistics \(mean, std, feature rankings\) to contaminate the training process. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
584 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 251 0 R
/E (regression\): Provides unbiased generalization estimate; outer fold test data is NEVER seen during inner HPO )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
585 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 251 0 R
/E (evaluate configurations only on inner folds; outer test data remains sealed )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
